.TH PARCHPROBE 1 "October 2026" "Parch GNU/Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
parchprobe \- hardware driver detection and configuration tool for Parch GNU/Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B parchprobe
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBparchprobe\fR is the native hardware driver management tool for Parch GNU/Linux.
It enumerates hardware devices present on the system over PCI and USB buses via sysfs,
matches them against a declarative database of hardware configurations, and performs
safe, automated driver installation and removal transactions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List driver configurations available for currently detected hardware on the system.
This is the default command if none is specified.
.TP
.B list-all
List all driver configurations available in the database regardless of connected hardware.
.TP
.B list-installed
List all driver configurations currently installed on the system according to the state database.
.TP
.B list-hardware
List all detected PCI and USB devices along with their vendor, device, and class IDs.
.TP
.BI install " <bus> <config...>"
Install one or more driver configurations for the specified bus (\fBpci\fR or \fBusb\fR).
Requires superuser privileges (root).
.TP
.BI remove " <bus> <config...>"
Remove one or more installed driver configurations for the specified bus (\fBpci\fR or \fBusb\fR).
Requires superuser privileges (root).
.TP
.BI install-custom " <bus> <path>"
Install a custom driver configuration from the specified directory containing a \fBPROBECONFIG\fR file.
Requires superuser privileges (root).
.TP
.BI auto " <bus> <free|nonfree> <classid>"
Automatically select and install the highest priority driver configuration for devices
matching the given device class (e.g. \fB0300\fR for graphics).
Requires superuser privileges (root).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-pci
Limit queries and operations to the PCI bus.
.TP
.B \-\-usb
Limit queries and operations to the USB bus.
.TP
.B \-\-detail
Display verbose information for devices and configurations.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Force reinstallation of an already installed configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON output on standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-pmroot " <path>"
Specify the root directory for package manager operations.
.TP
.BI \-\-pmconfig " <path>"
Specify an alternative configuration file for the package manager.
.TP
.BI \-\-pmcachedir " <path>"
Specify an alternative package cache directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display program version and license information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/parchprobe/db/
System driver database directory containing hardware definitions and hooks.
.TP
.I /var/lib/parchprobe/state.toml
Record of currently installed hardware driver configurations.
.TP
.I /etc/parchprobe-x86_64.conf
System configuration overrides, such as disabling multilib (lib32) driver packages.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PARCHPROBE_DB
Override the directory path for the driver database.
.TP
.B PARCHPROBE_STATE
Override the path to the installed state file.
.TP
.B PARCHPROBE_SYSFS
Override the root sysfs path (useful for testing or chroot environments).
